        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of Washington, Texas Christian University\n- People: Theodore Garland Jr., Addison Clark, Randolph Clark, Raymond B. Huey\n- Places: Seattle, Washington, Fort Worth, Texas\n- Topics: university founding, postdoctoral training\n\nFacts:\n- The University of Washington is a public flagship research university in Seattle, Washington, and it was established in 1861.\n- Texas Christian University was established in 1873 in Fort Worth, Texas, by Addison Clark and Randolph Clark as AddRan Male & Female College.\n- Texas Christian University is a private, coeducational university in Fort Worth, Texas.\n- Theodore Garland Jr. later completed postdoctoral training at the University of Washington with Raymond B. Huey.",
